From 524c6178777379c867eebcde2e498c5b13af11a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FuSan21 <FuSan21@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:05:26 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] LTW: Remote Task (Link to Windows "Apps"), scenario 0

Port of OnePlus RemoteTaskHandlerManager/RemoteTaskHandler for the
client-called launch: Link to Windows starts an app with options
deviceintegration:remotetask.{launchOption=32, uuid, security.token}.

- ActivityTaskManagerService.startActivityAsUser: before the options are
  parsed, LtwRemoteTaskManager.redirectLaunch checks the token set by
  deviceintegrationservice, creates a trusted virtual display
  MS_VIRTUAL_DISPLAY<n> (OnePlus flags) and sets
  android.activity.launchDisplayId; the normal launch path does the rest.
- activateRemoteTask(IServiceRemoteTaskInstance) is broadcast;
  deviceintegrationservice reads the display id from getBundle() and
  hands the encoder surface via updateSurface -> VirtualDisplay.setSurface.
- Task removal / PC close (removeRemoteTask) releases the display and
  reports notifyRemoteTaskRemoved.
- CrossDeviceService uses LtwRemoteTaskManager as its RemoteTaskHost.

Not yet: app-to-app/edge/duplicate/MD<->VD scenarios, PendingIntent
(notification) launches, secure-content and orientation reporting.
